drumee-schemas (2.7.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * Upgrade the MariaDB system tables to the running server version before
    populate runs, instead of letting Debian do it concurrently. The seed carries
    the system tables of whatever server produced it, so a restore onto a
    different version has mariadb-upgrade rewriting mysql.proc while populate is
    loading routines into it. The two deadlock on that table, and because
    lock_wait_timeout defaults to 86400 the install does not fail — it hangs for a
    day, indistinguishable from a slow restore.
  * Stop fetching initial content over the network during populate. The wallpaper
    and tutorial import reached a host that no longer resolves, and the failure
    path raised a ReferenceError instead of being skipped, aborting database
    initialization and leaving the package half-configured.
  * Fix the factory-pool guard, which counted system accounts through a column
    that has never existed. The query always errored, the error was swallowed into
    a zero, and the warning therefore fired on every install — including healthy
    ones whose pool count in the same message contradicted it.

 -- Somanos Sar <somanos.sar@drumee.com>  Fri, 31 Jul 2026 15:46:31 +0200

